***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          PATTERNNE

*   Problem :
*   *********
*   A nonlinear suystem arising from pattern formation.
*   This is a nonlinear equation variant of PATTERNLS

*   Source: 
*   D.J. Hill, J.J. Bramurger and D.J.B. Lloyd,
*   "Approximate localised dihedral patterns near a Turing instability",
*   Nonlinearity, vol. 36(5), pp. 2567-, 2023.

*   See also SIAM NEWS 57(5) June 2024

*   SIF input: Nick Gould, July 2024
*   Updated to improve processing, Pim Heeman, May 2026.

*   classification NQR2-AN-V-V

*   m is the order of dihedral symmetry

*IE m                   2              $-PARAMETER     original value
*IE m                   3              $-PARAMETER
*IE m                   4              $-PARAMETER
*IE m                   5              $-PARAMETER
 IE m                   6              $-PARAMETER

 RI M         m

*   N is the order of series expansion

*IE N                   10             $-PARAMETER     original value
*IE N                   100            $-PARAMETER
 IE N                   1000           $-PARAMETER

*   Define useful parameters

 IE 0                   0
 IE 1                   1
 IE 2                   2
 RE 2.0                 2.0
 RE 3.0                 3.0

* approximation of pi

 RF PI/4      ARCTAN    1.0
 RM PI        PI/4      4.0
 R/ PI/3      PI                       3.0
 R* MPI/3     M                        PI/3

VARIABLES

 DO n         0                        N
 X  a(n)
 ND

GROUPS

 DO n         0                        N
 XE c(n)      a(n)      -1.0
 ND

BOUNDS

 FR PATTERNNE 'DEFAULT'

START POINT

 XV PATTERNNE 'DEFAULT' 1.0

ELEMENT TYPE

 EV PROD      U
 EV PROD      V

ELEMENT USES

 XT 'DEFAULT' PROD

 DO i         0                        N
 DO j         0                        N
 ZV E(i,j)    U                        a(i)
 ZV E(i,j)    V                        a(j)
 ND

GROUP USES

 DO n         0                        N
 I- N-n       N                        n

 DO j         1                        N-n
 I+ n+j       n                        j
 I- n-j       n                        j
 RI rn-j      n-j
 R* arg       MPI/3                    rn-j
 R( carg      COS                      arg
 R* 2carg     2.0                      carg
 ZE c(n)      E(j,n+j)                 2carg
 OD j

 DO j         0                        n
 I* 2j        2                        j
 I- n-j       n                        j
 I- n-2j      n                        2j
 RI rn-2j     n-2j
 R* arg       MPI/3                    rn-2j
 R( carg      COS                      arg
 ZE c(n)      E(j,n-j)                 carg
 OD j

 ND

OBJECT BOUND

*   Solution

*LO SOLTN               0.0

ENDATA

***********************
* SET UP THE FUNCTION *
* AND RANGE ROUTINES  *
***********************

ELEMENTS      PATTERNNE

INDIVIDUALS

 T  PROD
 F                      U * V
 G  U                   V
 G  V                   U
 H  U         V         1.0

ENDATA
